* SEAT DECISIONS on the memory-stage row path (talked out under the recipe/bags model, 2026-11-07; overrulable):
(a) The stage law also holds on READ: a native page edit or a peer's merged change reaches no meme door, so the stage's readers (the L11 cold-boot index filter over the daemon wiki's composed recipe view, every stage reader) treat a row whose title disagrees with its row-key as a named fork, never a row; the backstop writes its refusal as a diagnostic tiddler in the working bag, not only a log line. Owed on L11 (+ meme-backstop).
(b) Concurrent same-key edits on two devices of the face (one row, one tiddler, in the face's working bag) surface, never resolve silently: stage readers read the CRDT's conflict set on the row's text and show both sides (the talk-story conflict-surfacing practice). Measure first how the island stores a tiddler's text field. Owed on L12/L11 before multi-device dogfooding.
(c) A burned stage row raises a kāpae in the working bag (kapae.mem law: an exclusion gesture raises a kāpae, never retracts to absent), so it shadows a lower-layer or re-poured copy; the disk projection must carry kāpae records and the re-pour must pour them, so a re-found never resurrects a burned memory. Measure whether projection writes kāpae today. GATES L19 (the flat memories move in).
(d) Two distinct memories choosing one readable key: authoring discipline (L19 class/slug) plus placeMeme's baseHash refusal; no new mechanism.
Durability beyond this machine: stage rows stay in the kahua working projection under the kept state root (cleartext only on disk + live wiki), never pushed to git; off-machine durability rides the vault backup door. Parity with today's flat memories (~/.claude, not in git).
* SEAT DECISIONS, trued for the layers ABOVE working (drafts, session/slot and other upper layers; operator note 2026-11-07):
(a') The stage law reads at the WORKING seam, where a row becomes a row: drafts and other upper layers hold work in progress (a rename mid-edit may disagree with its row-key legitimately), so stage readers and the L11 index read working + canon, never drafts, and the fork rule applies there.
(b') Concurrency catches at the draft -> working save, not as a CRDT conflict after the fact: a save from a draft carries the base the draft opened on (the meme doors' baseHash, extended to the native save path); a moved base refuses the save and keeps the draft standing beside the new working row (both visible), never a silent winner. The CRDT conflict read stays the backstop for writes that skip a draft.
(c') A burn must govern the layers above it too: raising the kāpae in working also discards or shadows open drafts and upper-layer copies of that row (a stale or synced draft must not re-surface a burned memory in the composed view); exports and re-pours carry the working layer and its kāpae records only, never drafts.
Measure: do drafts or session layers sync across a face's devices (if they do, (b') and (c') hold across devices too).
* MEASURED (Luna read seat, 2026-11-07; /home/joshu/.lares-scratch/dogfood-proof/seats/luna-measure/final.md), trues the stage-path decisions:
*# Daemon wiki recipe, top to bottom: temp -> draft -> personal -> working -> daemon canon -> kahua bag -> library bags -> oracle (wiki-recipe.ts:347-374); a kāpae shadows downward only (island-adaptor.ts:1115-1133) => (c') upward discard of drafts on a burn STANDS as owed.
*# DiskProjector unlinks a deleted record and writes no kāpae file (disk-projector.ts:693-702); ingest-back reads none => (c) CONFIRMED GAP: a re-pour of an old export resurrects a burned row. The projection writes kāpae records (or the export carries the burns) BEFORE L19.
*# text rests as a whole scalar (stored-value.ts:4-21); `readParallelDrafts` already surfaces concurrent values via getConflicts (parallel-drafts.ts) => (b) mostly BUILT: stage readers read through readParallelDrafts.
*# Drafts sync across a seated face's fleet (wiki-recipe.ts:149-160); temp stays local => (b')/(c') hold across devices.
*# The native draft save carries captured Automerge heads as its writeFamily base (island-adaptor.ts:1317-1330) => (b') the heads base IS the native save's base; no baseHash bolt-on, and a moved base surfaces through parallel drafts.
* kapae-disk (PR #205, 0cf54631d): seat decisions (overrulable): (1) the watcher sends .kapae shadows like carriers (owed row; both ends no-op a repeat); (2) a tombstone raised while the projector stood stopped writes no shadow at boot (owed row, pre-existing gap); (3) titles ingest-back cannot address (foreign titles, FileSystemPaths rules) get no usable shadow (named limit); (4) ACCEPTED: rename re-link uses removeIn (relocation retracts to absent per kapae.mem; a lower copy surfaces).
* dogfood-proof SHIP owed P3s: unset LAR_BAGS LAR_GENESIS in tools/dogfood-proof.sh; stage-row gate raw-string prefix and /path children collisions (read-side law covers); corepack fetch under fresh HOME.

